{"shortDescription":"MONTRÉAL, Oct. 13, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- NioBay Metals Inc. (“NioBay” or the “Company”) (TSX-V: NBY) OTCQB:NBYCF is proud to announce the initial results from the 2026 summer-autumn drilling campaign (the “2026 Campaign”) at the Crevier niobium (Nb) and tantalum (Ta) project (the “Crevier Projec…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["MONTRÉAL, Oct. 13, 2026 ",{"type":"url","params":{"url":"https://www.globenewswire.com","linkText":"(GLOBE NEWSWIRE)"}}," -- NioBay Metals Inc. (“NioBay” or the “Company”) (TSX-V: NBY) ","OTCQB:NBYCF"," is proud to announce the initial results from the 2026 summer-autumn drilling campaign (the “2026 Campaign”) at the Crevier niobium (Nb) and tantalum (Ta) project (the “Crevier Project”), in which it holds an 80.2% interest. The Crevier Project is located approximately 50 km north of the town of Girardville and approximately 150 km from the Niobec Mine. It is situated within the Nitassinan (or ancestral territory) of the Pekuakamiulnuatsh, whose main population center is Mashteuiatsh."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Highlights"]}]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":["The Company commenced a 10,000-meter drilling campaign in mid-June."]},{"type":"*","children":["The work involves: ",{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":["Drilling the northern sector, which showed higher tantalum grades during the 2023 program;"]},{"type":"*","children":["Drilling to increase resources in the southern extension (following up on 2025 work);"]},{"type":"*","children":["Drilling to test dikes at depth."]}]}," "]}]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Summary of Results"]}]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":["Tantalum intersections exceeding the deposit's average grade were obtained in the first 13 holes received. The data collected will be used to update the resource estimate following this drilling campaign."]},{"type":"*","c